\section*{Abstract}
The Continuous Yield Propulsion Core (CYPC-1) is a propulsion system derived
from the ACE-9K conservation and stability engine. CYPC-1 converts
information-density pressure fields into directed thrust while maintaining
structural, dynamical, and topological stability under extreme gradient
conditions. This document defines subsystem architecture, governing equations,
and a propulsion-specific stress-testing dossier.

\section{System Overview}
CYPC-1 integrates four ACE-9K layers into a unified propulsion pipeline:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item QP-Core: Information-density pressure generation
    \item SRK: Structural resistance and yield control
    \item FDE: Force propagation and thrust vectoring
    \item SFM: Global stability and failure manifold evaluation
\end{enumerate}

The system operates in Continuous Yield Mode, ensuring thrust generation without
structural or topological collapse.

\section{Layer I: QP-Core (Pressure Generation)}
Pressure is defined as:
\[
P(x) = \nabla \rho(x),
\]
with coupling:
\[
\Gamma_P = \frac{\partial}{\partial x^\mu} \log \rho(x^\mu).
\]

\subsection*{Propulsion Role}
The QP-Core shapes $\rho(x)$ to produce a controlled pressure field $P(x)$,
forming the intake and compression stage of CYPC-1.

\section{Layer II: SRK (Structural Resistance Kernel)}
Stress tensor:
\[
\sigma_{ij} = C_{ijkl}\epsilon_{kl},
\]
yield function:
\[
f_{\text{yield}} = \sqrt{\sigma_{ij}\sigma^{ij}} - \sigma_{\text{crit}}.
\]

\subsection*{Propulsion Role}
The SRK ensures the chamber and nozzle geometry remain below yield under
high-gradient pressure fields.

\section{Layer III: FDE (Force Dynamics Engine)}
Thrust propagation governed by:
\[
M\ddot{x}^\mu + D\dot{x}^\mu + Kx^\mu = F^\mu.
\]

\subsection*{Propulsion Role}
The FDE converts pressure gradients into directed thrust. The nozzle geometry
and magnetic/plasma shaping define $K$ and $D$.

\section{Layer IV: SFM (Stability--Failure Manifold)}
Global stability condition:
\[
\lambda_{\max}(K - \Gamma_P) < 0.
\]

\subsection*{Propulsion Role}
The SFM ensures thrust generation remains within a globally stable manifold,
preventing catastrophic instability.

\section{Conservation Layer}
CYPC-1 inherits ACE-9K conservation checks:
\[
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0, \qquad 
\nabla_\mu J^\mu = 0,
\]
and preserves the topological metric-innate helicity invariant:
\[
\frac{dH_{\text{metric}}}{dt} \approx 0.
\]

\section{Propulsion Pipeline: Continuous Yield Mode}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Ingest fuel/plasma/field as $\rho(x)$.
    \item Generate pressure field $P(x)$ via QP-Core.
    \item Evaluate structural limits via SRK.
    \item Solve thrust propagation via FDE.
    \item Evaluate global stability via SFM.
    \item Validate conservation and invariant retention.
\end{enumerate}

